    "rename_date_utc": "2026-06-01",
    "definition": "R-Precision@K = (1/Q) * sum_{q in Q} r_q / min(K, R_q), where Q is the set of days with R_q > 0 positives, R_q is the count of positives on day q, r_q is the count of positives in the top-K picks on day q. Macro-averaged across days, equal weight per day. K is fixed (per-day variable-K under the legacy 'weighted R-precision' metric used the per-day R(d) as K; macro-averaged R-Precision@K uses a fixed K and the min(K, R_q) denominator for achievability). See .claude/memories/project-r-precision-methodology.md for the full definition and the relationship to the legacy metric.",
